From: Caboose <caboose@local>
Subject: [PATCH 96/96] Offer VK_EXT_vertex_attribute_divisor alongside the KHR name

The device extension list passed VK_KHR_vertex_attribute_divisor but not the EXT name it
was promoted from. Zink takes vertex attribute divisors from the EXT name alone, so on the
driver it had no instanced arrays: OpenGL 3.2 and OpenGL ES 2.0, where the same zink on
the same Vulkan implementation has 4.6 and ES 3.2. An application that asks for ES 3.0
without falling back, such as Chromium's and CEF's GPU process, then failed to start
(eglCreateContext: EGL_BAD_ATTRIBUTE). The EXT name is passed when the host has it; its
structures are the KHR ones' aliases, which the encoder already carries.
---
diff --git a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
--- a/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
+++ b/src/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp
@@ -2561,6 +2561,8 @@
         "VK_EXT_depth_clip_enable",
         "VK_KHR_create_renderpass2",
         "VK_KHR_vertex_attribute_divisor",
+        // Caboose: zink takes divisors from the EXT name only (GL 3.3 and ES 3.0 need them).
+        "VK_EXT_vertex_attribute_divisor",
         "VK_EXT_host_query_reset",
         "VK_EXT_blend_operation_advanced",
         "VK_EXT_frame_boundary",
